    {
      "id": "DC_kwDOKrJqmc4AxCRg",
      "body": "rayhunter doesn't perform any active surveying, it captures data from regular usage of your modem and looks for activity that looks similar to IMSI catchers. i don't think there's a clear answer to whether it's better to move around or to stand still while rayhunter is active. from my experience, rayhunter can have false-positives when entering and exiting subway tunnels, probably because of (legitimate) femtocells.",
      "author": {
        "login": "untitaker",
        "avatar_url": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/837573?u=4b106f1ba83b3028677a861efe31c46d703e77ff&v=4",
