      "id": "DC_kwDOKrJqmc4AxCV9",
      "body": "Okay, I was thinking of putting it on my drone but also wanted to use an active sim w/ service so that I could reach the Pi that's on board as well via the modem. Assuming that the usb connection from the Orbit can act as a USB ethernet connection to the Pi, otherwise I guess I'd use the WiFi from the hotspot. I just wasn't certain if RayHunter would at any point interfere with the active service. ",
      "author": {
        "login": "alphafox02",
        "avatar_url": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/44436101?v=4",
        "url": "https://github.com/alphafox02"
      },
      "created_at": "2025-04-16T13:00:23Z",
      "updated_at": "2025-04-16T13:00:23Z",
      "is_answer": false,
      "replies": [
        {
          "id": "DC_kwDOKrJqmc4A5Jh0",
          "body": "This is from April, but this seems important to note. I wouldn't use the modem with an active plan, attached to a drone. Same reason I would put a phone on a weather balloon operating as a aprs modem for ham radio telemetry in airplane mode. \r\nhttps://www.ecfr.gov/current/title-47/chapter-I/subchapter-B/part-22/subpart-H/section-22.925\r\n\r\n\r\n```\r\n22.925 Prohibition on airborne operation of cellular telephones.\r\n\r\n\r\nCellular telephones installed in or carried aboard airplanes, balloons or any other type of aircraft must not be \r\noperated while such aircraft are airborne (not touching the ground). When any aircraft leaves the ground, all \r\ncellular telephones on board that aircraft must be turned off. The following notice must be posted on or near \r\neach cellular telephone installed in any aircraft:\r\n\r\n\r\n“The use of cellular telephones while this aircraft is airborne is prohibited by FCC rules, and the violation of \r\nthis rule could result in suspension of service and/or a fine. The use of cellular telephones while this aircraft is \r\non the ground is subject to FAA regulations.\r\n```\r\n\r\nNot that people don't leave their phones on without airplane mode on planes etc every day, but interfacing with a meshtastic or something is probably a better option imho",
          "author": {
            "login": "deathzombee",
            "avatar_url": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8412573?u=67483675c9a808804846bb9884d6e8f07c4c3f57&v=4",
            "url": "https://github.com/deathzombee"
          },
